    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Mason Estates take great pleasure in introducing 4 Grove Lawn to the market. A substantial three-bedroom detached bungalow, enjoying a large private east facing rear garden, generous off-street parking to the front and an unusually wide side area incorporating a number of useful outbuildings. The property offers excellent scope for further development and extension, and will undoubtedly appeal to those looking for a spacious living space with the potential to create a substantial family home in this highly regarded residential location.\n\nInternally, the accommodation extends to approximately 131 sq. m. and is laid out over one level, offering well-proportioned and flexible accommodation throughout. The property comprises a welcoming entrance hall, spacious living room/dining area with large rear windows, a sitting room, kitchen, three bedrooms, and a main bathroom. To the side there is a large garage together with substantial storage and utility/outbuilding space, providing excellent additional storage options , a guest w.c., and a separate laundry room.\n\nOne of the outstanding features of No. 4 is the exceptional potential it offers for expansion. The generous rear garden provides considerable scope to extend the existing accommodation, subject of course to the necessary planning permission. There is also excellent potential within the existing roof space to create additional habitable accommodation. The attic space runs the length of the property, is approximately 2.8m at the apex of the roof, and, subject to planning and the necessary structural works, could provide a substantial attic conversion incorporating dormer windows to the side. There is precedent for this type of development on Grove Lawn, with numerous houses converting this space to usable attic space, while the property two doors up has undertaken a stunning modern dormer-style attic conversion. Any purchaser should satisfy themselves regarding the planning requirements and feasibility of any proposed works.\n\nTo the front there is a private walled garden with generous off-street parking. The extensive side areas provides further potential to extend. To the rear there is a large, private east facing garden, offering excellent scope for landscaping, outdoor entertaining and further extension of the existing accommodation.\n\nGrove Lawn is a mature and highly regarded residential location just off Grove Avenue in Blackrock. The property is within easy walking distance of both Blackrock and Stillorgan Villages, with their excellent selection of boutiques, restaurants, cafés, supermarkets and other amenities. There are excellent transport links close at hand, including the N.11 Quality Bus Corridor providing quick and convenient access to Dublin City Centre, while Blackrock DART station is also readily accessible.\n\nThe location is particularly well regarded for its choice of schools, with many of Dublin`s premier primary and secondary schools within easy reach, including Carysfort National School, Willow Park, Oatlands College, St. Andrew`s College, Blackrock College, Sion Hill, and other highly regarded schools in the surrounding area. UCD and the UCD Smurfit Business School are also close at hand.\n\nThe property is also ideally located for a wide range of recreational amenities, with numerous sports clubs, parks and leisure facilities in the surrounding Blackrock and Stillorgan areas.\n\nIn short, 4 Grove Lawn is a substantial detached bungalow occupying an excellent position in this mature and highly sought-after residential location. With spacious accommodation already in place, a large private east facing rear garden, extensive side outbuildings and considerable potential to extend to the rear and into the attic, this is a property that offers a rare opportunity to create a wonderful family home in one of South Dublin`s most popular residential areas. Viewing is highly recommended. To arrange a viewing please contact Ryan O`Shaughnessy or call the office on 01 2951001.\n\nACCOMMODATION\n\nTotal Floor Area: 131 sq. m. (1,410 sq. ft.) approximately\nExcluding porch, patio, laundry, storage, toilet, garage, utility/HP and fireplace areas as indicated on the floor plan.\n\nPORCH: 1.13m x 1.83m\nEnclosed entrance porch leading to the entrance hall.\n\nENTRANCE HALL: 3.93m x 7.50m\nExceptionally spacious entrance hall providing access to the principal accommodation.\n\nLIVING ROOM: 4.97m x 4.17m\nGenerous bright living room with feature fireplace and windows overlooking the front garden.\n\nDINING AREA: 3.44m x 3.53m\nWell-proportioned dining area, ideally positioned adjoining the living accommodation and with access to the rear patio and garden.\n\nSITTING ROOM: 3.34m x 4.26m\nSpacious additional reception room with excellent potential for a variety of uses.\n\nKITCHEN: 3.34m x 3.78m\nGood-sized kitchen with fitted floor and wall units and access to the side of the property.\n\nMASTER BEDROOM: 4.54m x 3.41m\nFine double bedroom overlooking the rear garden.\n\nBEDROOM 2: 3.96m x 3.41m\nGenerous double bedroom.\n\nBEDROOM 3: 3.97m x 3.38m\nFurther well-proportioned bedroom.\n\nSHOWER ROOM: 2.69m x 2.09m\nSpacious shower-room incorporating shower, w.c. and w.h.b.\n\nGUEST WC: 1.63m x 0.86m\nConvenient guest w.c.\n\nLAUNDRY ROOM: 1.63m x 1.56m\nSeparate laundry room with access to the side of the property.\n\nSTORAGE: 2.70m x 4.26m\nLarge storage area with excellent potential for a variety of uses.\n\nGARAGE: 2.70m x 5.08m\nGood-sized garage with access to the side of the property.\n\nSIDE OUTBUILDINGS / UTILITY AREA\nThe property benefits from an unusually generous side area incorporating a number of useful outbuildings, together with the garage, storage and utility/HP areas. These provide excellent additional storage and considerable flexibility for the new owner.\n\nGARDENS\nFront: 15.4m x 9.1m\nPrivate front garden with generous off-street parking and access to both sides of the property and garage.\nRear: 14.8m x 15.1m\nLarge, private east facing rear garden with a patio area and excellent potential for landscaping and further extension, subject to the necessary planning permission."
      },
